WEBVTT

00:00.512 --> 00:03.815
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.915 --> 00:07.183
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.218 --> 00:10.753
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.788 --> 00:13.756
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.791 --> 00:17.259
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.295 --> 00:20.429
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.465 --> 00:21.964
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.000 --> 00:23.866
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.901 --> 00:25.538
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.080 --> 00:37.613
Hey.
What are you working on?

00:37.649 --> 00:40.916
Oh, just trying to make some
sense of these numbers.

00:42.587 --> 00:43.953
What the...
What did you hit?

00:43.988 --> 00:45.688
What happened to
my spreadsheet?

00:45.723 --> 00:49.191
What exactly was the endgame
if I hadn't walked in?

00:49.227 --> 00:51.460
Ugh, there's nothing worse
than grocery shopping

00:51.496 --> 00:52.696
on the day before
Thanksgiving.

00:54.232 --> 00:56.899
Yeah, that's the sound
a rich family's turkey makes.

00:56.934 --> 00:59.135
There's still a lot more
groceries in the car.

00:59.170 --> 01:01.203
Well, it's not a race.
Take a break.

01:01.239 --> 01:03.372
Ugh, if you knew
how close we were

01:03.408 --> 01:05.741
to putting you
down last year.

01:05.777 --> 01:07.076
Geez, what's her problem?

01:07.111 --> 01:08.678
Eh, Thanksgiving's
exhausting.

01:08.713 --> 01:10.012
You know what
she could use?

01:10.048 --> 01:12.248
A little sip
of that drink I invented.

01:12.283 --> 01:14.450
Hi! Stewie Griffin here
with my latest creation:

01:14.485 --> 01:16.686
Monster Energy Drink.
What is it? I don't know,

01:16.721 --> 01:19.021
but it's free from this truck
that stopped outside your work.

01:19.057 --> 01:21.257
Mix it with booze. Ever been
wide-awake-blacked-out?

01:21.292 --> 01:23.325
Ever try to jump over
a train on a bike?

01:23.361 --> 01:25.327
Ever bit the beak off a bird?
Monster Energy:

01:25.363 --> 01:27.363
put it in your body
and ask questions later.

01:27.398 --> 01:29.231
It's green, so it's nature.

01:32.670 --> 01:34.837
<i>We now return to Guy Friends.</i>

01:34.872 --> 01:36.472
So, you must
be pretty pumped.

01:36.507 --> 01:37.773
For what?

01:37.809 --> 01:39.141
Oh. Olympics.

01:39.177 --> 01:41.343
Oh, yeah. I guess
that's starting soon.

01:41.379 --> 01:43.145
I thought you were
a big Olympics guy.

01:43.181 --> 01:45.047
Yeah, I like 'em okay.

01:45.083 --> 01:47.116
Huh.

01:47.151 --> 01:48.951
♪ Guy friends ♪

01:48.986 --> 01:51.620
♪ A computer made us
roommates in college ♪

01:51.656 --> 01:52.621
♪ That's why we're friends ♪

01:52.657 --> 01:54.156
♪ Guy friends! ♪

01:54.192 --> 01:56.058
Mail's here.

01:56.094 --> 01:58.994
Any fliers of Hispanic women
running for city council?

01:59.030 --> 02:00.529
Yeah, there is.

02:00.565 --> 02:01.897
Thank you.

02:03.234 --> 02:05.534
Peter, you got a letter
from your sister Karen.

02:05.570 --> 02:07.369
What? You've got
a sister, Dad?

02:07.405 --> 02:08.938
How come we've
never met her?

02:08.973 --> 02:10.706
Is she a prim and proper
aunt

02:10.742 --> 02:12.808
or a big, fat,
dirty aunt?

02:12.844 --> 02:15.177
I have no obligation
to tell any of you anything.

02:15.213 --> 02:17.680
Mr. Griffin has shown good
faith in appearing here today

02:17.715 --> 02:19.148
and will not be subjected

02:19.183 --> 02:21.083
to this sort of
hostile interrogation.

02:21.119 --> 02:23.953
Your father doesn't like to
talk about his sister, Meg.

02:23.988 --> 02:25.955
They've never
really gotten along.

02:25.990 --> 02:27.757
Wow, Peter.
In all the years I've known you,

02:27.792 --> 02:28.958
you've never even
mentioned a sister.

02:28.993 --> 02:30.993
Big deal, I don't
talk about my sister.

02:31.028 --> 02:33.395
I also don't talk about
that tickling uncle.

02:33.431 --> 02:35.297
All right, Uncle Dan,
remember: no tickling.

02:35.333 --> 02:37.333
You got it.

02:39.604 --> 02:41.504
You didn't say anything
about Uncle Neil.

02:41.539 --> 02:43.472
Whose uncles are you?

02:43.508 --> 02:45.608
It says here your sister's
coming for Thanksgiving.

02:45.643 --> 02:47.243
She what?

02:47.278 --> 02:48.978
If we're having
guests, can I invite

02:49.013 --> 02:51.380
Rosario Vargas from
the third district,

02:51.415 --> 02:52.982
a leader you
can depend on?

02:53.017 --> 02:54.717
I don't want
Karen here.

02:54.752 --> 02:57.720
Peter, you've been avoiding
your sister for too long.

02:57.755 --> 02:59.822
Besides, she says she's been
having Thanksgiving

02:59.857 --> 03:01.757
with your mother for
the last 20 years.

03:01.793 --> 03:03.292
And now that your mom
has passed,

03:03.327 --> 03:05.561
she'd like to spend
Thanksgiving with you.

03:10.168 --> 03:11.634
No.

03:11.669 --> 03:13.502
Peter, Karen's coming
and that's that.

03:13.538 --> 03:15.905
How cool! I didn't
even know I had an aunt.

03:15.940 --> 03:17.506
I can't wait
to meet her.

03:17.542 --> 03:19.575
Look, I'm telling you guys,
it's gonna be a disaster.

03:19.610 --> 03:22.478
<i>Just like the alternate
ending of Back to the Future.</i>

03:22.513 --> 03:24.213
♪ ♪

03:27.451 --> 03:29.685
Well, if I'm gonna
disappear into nothing,

03:29.720 --> 03:31.320
I might as well bang my mom.

03:31.355 --> 03:33.088
Hey, Lorraine, wait up!

03:35.326 --> 03:37.426
Hi! My name's Marty!

03:37.461 --> 03:39.662
I'm in a picture!

03:39.697 --> 03:41.664
♪ ♪

03:41.699 --> 03:43.666
<i>To be contondered!</i>

03:48.973 --> 03:51.040
<i>We now return to The Cosby Show,</i>

03:51.075 --> 03:53.008
knowing what we know now.

04:19.437 --> 04:22.171
Huh. I was so busy
not seeing color,

04:22.206 --> 04:24.240
I didn't see the raping, either.

04:24.275 --> 04:26.542
Okay, everyone.
It'll be another hour

04:26.577 --> 04:29.645
before the turkey's done,
but I made more appetizers.

04:29.680 --> 04:33.082
Ooh, grape jelly on a Triscuit.
You're a whiz.

04:33.117 --> 04:35.084
Whoa, whoa, whoa, slow down.
Save your appetite.

04:35.119 --> 04:36.552
And don't think
I haven't noticed

04:36.587 --> 04:38.053
you've already had two drinks.

04:38.089 --> 04:40.222
You're, like, all the worst
parts of a girlfriend.

04:41.525 --> 04:43.192
Oh. That must be Karen.

04:43.227 --> 04:45.261
I'll get it. Aunt Karen?

04:45.296 --> 04:48.430
And you must be Meg.

04:48.466 --> 04:50.266
Do that to me!

04:54.639 --> 04:57.506
Wow, it's so cool that I've got
an aunt I didn't know about.

04:57.541 --> 05:00.409
Oh, Karen, I'm so happy
you could make it.

05:00.444 --> 05:03.579
Lois Pewterschmidt.
The one that got away.

05:03.614 --> 05:05.047
I'm just joshing, kid.

05:05.082 --> 05:06.682
Auntie's not a biscuit-bumper.

05:08.653 --> 05:10.519
I'm not, either!

05:11.656 --> 05:13.756
Peter, come say hello
to your sister.

05:13.791 --> 05:16.225
Fine.

05:16.260 --> 05:18.060
Hey, Karen.
Welcome to our...

05:18.095 --> 05:19.962
Bring it in, Pee Pee!

05:23.167 --> 05:24.533
I like her.

05:24.568 --> 05:28.370
Hello. I am City Councilwoman
Rosario Vargas.

05:28.406 --> 05:32.141
Quahog doesn't work if
it doesn't work for all of us.

05:32.176 --> 05:34.944
That's a beautiful
pantsuit, Ms. Vargas.

05:39.822 --> 05:41.121
Wow, Karen,
nice to meet you.

05:41.157 --> 05:42.656
I'm Glenn Quagmire.

05:42.692 --> 05:44.291
I didn't know
Peter even had a sister.

05:44.327 --> 05:46.327
What are you,
ashamed of me, Chin Nuts?

05:46.362 --> 05:49.563
Oh, my God. His chin kind
of does look like nuts.

05:49.599 --> 05:51.465
Ha, ha! I never
noticed that.

05:51.500 --> 05:53.167
How could you
not notice it?

05:53.202 --> 05:56.837
Watch this,
I-I'll punch him in the nuts.

05:56.872 --> 05:58.205
Eh, sort of clever.

05:58.240 --> 05:59.506
Wait a second. I know you.

05:59.542 --> 06:00.741
You're that lady wrestler.

06:00.776 --> 06:02.076
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
he's right.

06:02.111 --> 06:03.544
Hey, w-what do they
call you again?

06:03.579 --> 06:06.046
Heavy Flo.
You're Heavy Flo!

06:06.082 --> 06:07.915
In the flesh and blood.

06:07.950 --> 06:10.017
Gross.
Man, you're amazing.

06:10.052 --> 06:12.052
I remember when you called out
Andrea the Giant

06:12.088 --> 06:13.988
the day after September 11.

06:14.023 --> 06:16.223
What just happened was
a national tragedy,

06:16.258 --> 06:18.559
but it's nothing compared
to what I'm gonna do

06:18.594 --> 06:20.427
to Andrea the Giant!

06:20.463 --> 06:22.696
We will never forget
what happened yesterday,

06:22.732 --> 06:26.233
but you'll also never forget
what's gonna happen September 17

06:26.268 --> 06:29.236
at the Jack Witschi
Sports Arena!

06:29.271 --> 06:31.605
Peter, I can't believe you've
kept your sister a secret.

06:31.641 --> 06:33.007
She's amazing!

06:33.042 --> 06:34.408
Yeah, she's crazy strong.

06:34.443 --> 06:36.110
Like Superman on a date.

06:36.145 --> 06:38.545
Yeah, I wasn't here,
but I heard her scream,

06:38.581 --> 06:40.614
so I came flying in
and found her like this.

06:40.650 --> 06:42.449
It's weird.
Same cause of death

06:42.485 --> 06:44.918
as those three guys
in that local public bathroom.

06:44.954 --> 06:47.121
Unsolvable.

06:50.893 --> 06:53.394
Now do you see why I didn't
want Karen here, Lois?

06:53.429 --> 06:55.195
She terrorized me
my whole childhood.

06:55.231 --> 06:57.464
Now she's got to embarrass
me in front of my friends?

06:57.500 --> 06:59.366
Peter, Bonnie just
changed Joe on the table.

06:59.402 --> 07:00.934
What are you
worried about?

07:00.970 --> 07:03.370
Still, I don't want
to go back out there.

07:03.406 --> 07:04.972
Look, I know
you've had your differences,

07:05.007 --> 07:06.140
but Karen's your sister.

07:06.175 --> 07:07.975
And you're grown-ups now.

07:08.010 --> 07:11.145
Can't you just go out there
and pretend to have a good time?

07:11.180 --> 07:12.479
Fine, I'll play along.

07:12.515 --> 07:14.648
I guess I've lied before.

07:17.086 --> 07:18.986
Where you going?
Home.

07:19.021 --> 07:20.487
Where's home?

07:20.523 --> 07:22.156
The White House.

07:25.928 --> 07:27.428
Okay, I'm here.
This is my house.

07:27.463 --> 07:29.263
You can go now.
Thanks for taking me home.

07:29.298 --> 07:30.431
Go ahead, go inside.

07:30.466 --> 07:31.999
I will.
You can drive away now.

07:32.034 --> 07:34.735
No, no, I-I want to make
sure you get inside safe.

07:34.770 --> 07:36.670
Yeah, but I-I got to look
through the mail first.

07:36.706 --> 07:38.172
You know how it is.
Really, I insist.

07:38.207 --> 07:39.807
I-It's totally okay. Go.

07:39.842 --> 07:41.975
At this point, it's more
about me than it is you.

07:42.011 --> 07:43.310
It's a bad
neighborhood.

07:43.345 --> 07:44.912
If I don't see
you go inside,

07:44.947 --> 07:46.947
I'll be thinking
about it all night.

08:03.365 --> 08:06.366
Uh... come on in,
Mr. President!

08:19.715 --> 08:22.816
And then, so I'm like, "Peter,
how was I supposed to know

08:22.852 --> 08:25.119
you didn't want your teammates
to know you wore a bra?"

08:27.022 --> 08:29.623
It was a custom-designed
sports halter top.

08:29.658 --> 08:31.225
More stories!
More stories!

08:31.260 --> 08:33.494
Hey, tell one where
Peter is a nincompoop

08:33.529 --> 08:34.995
or maybe a Silly Billy.

08:36.532 --> 08:37.898
Oh, man.

08:37.933 --> 08:39.333
Okay, let's just
carve the turkey.

08:39.368 --> 08:40.901
Oh, Aunt Karen
already carved it.

08:40.936 --> 08:42.836
She did?
But that's my thing.

08:42.872 --> 08:45.839
I always do my "are you a leg
man or a breast man" joke.

08:45.875 --> 08:47.074
Aunt Karen
did that, too.

08:47.109 --> 08:48.542
It was hilarious.

08:48.577 --> 08:50.978
I never really got it
until she said it.

08:51.013 --> 08:52.379
Ha, ha!

08:54.250 --> 08:55.783
Hey, Karen,
later you got to show us

08:55.818 --> 08:57.117
some of your wrestling holds.

08:57.153 --> 08:59.193
Yeah, what's that trademark
finishing move of yours?

08:59.221 --> 09:00.521
The Toxic Shock.

09:00.556 --> 09:02.022
Oh, yeah,
that move is badass!

09:02.057 --> 09:04.424
You're awesome.
Know what else is awesome?

09:04.460 --> 09:06.393
This stuffing.
Thank you, Glenn.

09:06.428 --> 09:07.928
You're welcome.
I'm in a good mood.

09:07.963 --> 09:09.830
Sure, what the hell,
I'll show you my moves.

09:09.865 --> 09:11.198
Maybe after dinner.

09:11.233 --> 09:13.367
No, no, no. The family
football game is after dinner.

09:13.402 --> 09:14.968
We do it every year!

09:15.004 --> 09:16.970
Peter, calm down.
You're making a scene.

09:17.006 --> 09:19.907
It's not my fault, Lois.
She's ruining Thanksgiving!

09:19.942 --> 09:22.709
The way Tim Burton
ruined the Fourth of July!

09:27.149 --> 09:30.851
♪ Spooky! Happy!
Spooky! Happy! ♪

09:30.886 --> 09:32.319
♪ Weirdness! Weirdness! ♪

09:32.354 --> 09:34.054
♪ Spooky! Happy! ♪

09:34.089 --> 09:35.989
♪ La, la, la! ♪

09:36.025 --> 09:37.624
♪ Weirdness, weirdness ♪

09:37.660 --> 09:39.359
♪ Patriotic weirdness ♪

09:39.395 --> 09:41.028
♪ Barbecuing human heads ♪

09:41.063 --> 09:42.663
♪ Every president is dead ♪

09:42.698 --> 09:44.464
♪ Everybody's gonna die ♪

09:44.500 --> 09:46.333
♪ Have a dark and dead July! ♪

09:48.137 --> 09:52.940
Fat chicks with black hair
get tattoos of me!

10:01.250 --> 10:02.916
God, I love this time of year.

10:02.952 --> 10:05.252
It's just past
all the amazing colors of fall,

10:05.287 --> 10:07.120
and before the white of winter.

10:07.156 --> 10:09.089
Just brown and gray.

10:09.124 --> 10:10.457
Magical.

10:10.492 --> 10:11.925
All right, let's do this.

10:11.961 --> 10:13.460
All right, listen up,
I'm the captain.

10:13.495 --> 10:15.596
The teams are chosen by
a lottery system where...

10:15.631 --> 10:17.331
Aunt Karen, can I
be on your team?

10:17.366 --> 10:18.498
Yeah, yeah, me, too!

10:18.534 --> 10:20.300
Uh, yeah, sure,
I'll take, uh,

10:20.336 --> 10:23.470
Meg, Skinny,
Hot Chocolate and The Bus.

10:23.505 --> 10:24.905
Pee Pee, you get
the crumbs.

10:24.940 --> 10:26.073
Let's go.

10:26.108 --> 10:27.574
All right, let's do it, Pop!

10:27.610 --> 10:29.843
I'm gonna make some
sports points for you!

10:29.879 --> 10:31.044
We'll kick off.

10:33.949 --> 10:34.915
Hey, time-out!

10:34.950 --> 10:36.283
Did anyone tape the parade?

10:36.318 --> 10:38.352
Please tell me
someone taped the parade!

10:43.893 --> 10:46.426
Oh, my God! She's
doing The Toxic Shock!

10:55.471 --> 11:00.607
Y-Y-You're a j-jerk, K-K-Karen!

11:00.643 --> 11:02.075
What the hell was that?

11:02.111 --> 11:03.443
That's his stutter.

11:03.479 --> 11:06.046
And whenever he stutters,
he usually pees his pants.

11:06.081 --> 11:09.249
N-No, I... d-d-don't.

11:10.920 --> 11:12.853
Oh.

11:14.990 --> 11:16.423
So this is football.

11:16.458 --> 11:17.758
I like it.

11:24.400 --> 11:26.033
Hi, Dad.

11:26.068 --> 11:28.535
Look, I-I just want you to know,
I feel bad about what happened

11:28.570 --> 11:30.237
with you and Aunt Karen
the other day.

11:30.272 --> 11:33.040
Oh, you mean when she put me in
that no-bottom James Bond chair

11:33.075 --> 11:34.508
and assaulted my grundle?

11:34.543 --> 11:35.943
I didn't even
know about that.

11:35.978 --> 11:38.378
Well, that's 'cause
it didn't happen.

11:38.414 --> 11:40.414
I'd kick her ass if she
tried something like that!

11:40.449 --> 11:43.750
Dad, stop. Even I can see
that your sister's a huge bully.

11:43.786 --> 11:46.820
And trust me, I know more about
getting bullied than anyone.

11:46.855 --> 11:49.089
You do? How?

11:49.124 --> 11:52.960
♪ Celebrate good times,
come on ♪

11:52.995 --> 11:54.962
♪ Let's celebrate ♪

11:54.997 --> 11:56.596
♪ Ooh, ooh-ooh, ooh ♪

11:56.632 --> 12:00.968
♪ Celebrate good times,
come on. ♪

12:02.304 --> 12:04.538
Man, I love that song.

12:04.573 --> 12:06.640
Dad, what I'm trying
to tell you is,

12:06.675 --> 12:09.209
I now see why you've been
so tough on me all these years.

12:09.244 --> 12:10.610
'Cause it makes
my friends laugh?

12:10.646 --> 12:12.946
No, because that's how
Aunt Karen treated you

12:12.982 --> 12:14.114
when you were a kid.

12:15.718 --> 12:18.452
That's right. And that's why
you need to confront Karen.

12:18.487 --> 12:20.320
Oh, no. Oh, no.
No, I can't do that.

12:20.356 --> 12:22.089
I tried for years
to stand up to her.

12:22.124 --> 12:23.124
Nothing ever worked.

12:23.158 --> 12:24.624
What, so now
you're gonna quit?

12:24.660 --> 12:25.625
You can't quit.

12:25.661 --> 12:27.661
What if Muhammad Ali had quit?

12:27.696 --> 12:29.663
Ah, my grandchildren!

12:29.698 --> 12:31.531
Who would like me
to read them a book,

12:31.567 --> 12:33.834
or maybe paint their name
on a grain of rice?

12:33.869 --> 12:35.769
Honey, dinnertime!

12:35.804 --> 12:37.070
Ah, my favorite.

12:37.106 --> 12:38.839
Hot soup.

12:38.874 --> 12:40.540
Right in there.

12:40.576 --> 12:42.909
Dad, I know you can
stand up to Aunt Karen.

12:42.945 --> 12:46.179
And maybe if you finally do,
she'll stop terrorizing you,

12:46.215 --> 12:48.181
and you won't have to
take it out on me

12:48.217 --> 12:49.449
for the rest of my life.

12:49.485 --> 12:51.084
You know what, Meg?

12:51.120 --> 12:53.153
You're right!
I'm gonna do it!

12:53.188 --> 12:54.154
You are?

12:54.189 --> 12:55.155
Damn right!

12:55.190 --> 12:56.390
Yay, Dad!

12:56.425 --> 12:58.358
I am gonna become
a lady wrestler

12:58.394 --> 13:00.727
and defeat Heavy Flo
in the ring.

13:00.763 --> 13:02.295
Wait. What?! No! What?!

13:02.331 --> 13:03.730
I meant go talk to her.

13:03.766 --> 13:05.665
Nope, it's got to be a
lady wrestling match.

13:05.701 --> 13:07.334
Hey, Meg,
Thanksgiving's over.

13:07.369 --> 13:10.203
Come help me
with the Christmas decorations.

13:10.239 --> 13:12.072
Meg! Help me with
the Christmas decorations!

13:18.187 --> 13:19.920
Comments? Questions?

13:19.956 --> 13:21.088
What the hell are you...

13:21.124 --> 13:22.656
I'm sorry. Chris had
his hand up first.

13:22.692 --> 13:23.657
Chris?

13:23.693 --> 13:25.493
What's the capital
of Maryland?

13:25.528 --> 13:27.495
I do not know, but that's
a very good question.

13:27.530 --> 13:28.496
Now, Lois?

13:28.531 --> 13:30.631
Peter, what the hell
are you doing?!

13:30.666 --> 13:32.233
First, it's not Peter.

13:32.268 --> 13:34.935
When I am in this outfit,
I am Maxi Paddy,

13:34.971 --> 13:37.338
the fiercest enemy of Heavy Flo.

13:37.373 --> 13:39.273
Peter, you look--
okay, that's clever--

13:39.308 --> 13:41.008
but, Peter,
you look ridiculous.

13:41.043 --> 13:42.109
Take that off.

13:42.145 --> 13:43.911
If you want to settle things
with your sister,

13:43.946 --> 13:45.246
just go talk to her.

13:45.281 --> 13:47.782
No, Lois, the only way to
settle a family dispute

13:47.817 --> 13:49.083
is in the cage.

13:49.118 --> 13:50.217
I mean, you don't understand.

13:50.253 --> 13:51.452
Karen made me feel worse than

13:51.487 --> 13:53.788
a guy getting cut
from a baseball team.

13:53.823 --> 13:55.055
You wanted to
see me, Coach?

13:55.091 --> 13:57.191
I'm sorry, Kyle.
You can't do this boring,

13:57.226 --> 13:58.926
stupid thing with us.

14:02.498 --> 14:05.266
All right, Peter,
your sister's the real deal.

14:05.301 --> 14:08.035
So I arranged for you
to get some combat pointers

14:08.070 --> 14:10.704
from my old buddy,
Steven Seagal.

14:10.740 --> 14:13.607
Uh, this... this fat guy?

14:13.643 --> 14:16.010
Yup. Go on, ask him anything.

14:16.045 --> 14:17.645
How... how did...?

14:17.680 --> 14:19.346
Uh, why-why you so fat?

14:19.382 --> 14:21.849
Okay, ask him about
anything but his weight.

14:21.884 --> 14:23.117
Uh...

14:23.152 --> 14:25.986
uh, you act Asian,
you look Native American,

14:26.022 --> 14:27.888
your name is possibly Jewish.

14:27.924 --> 14:29.390
What are you?

14:29.425 --> 14:30.791
He fat.

14:32.328 --> 14:34.562
All right, Peter,
most professional wrestlers

14:34.597 --> 14:36.831
become addicted to painkillers
at some point.

14:36.866 --> 14:39.266
So I figure,
why don't we just start now?

14:39.302 --> 14:42.136
Uh... okay,
yeah, I'm in.

14:42.171 --> 14:43.404
Where you getting
all these?

14:43.439 --> 14:45.005
Stepdaughter's purse.

14:45.041 --> 14:47.208
Ain't my problem.

14:47.243 --> 14:52.012
Man, I love putting my hand down
my pants when I'm on drugs.

14:52.048 --> 14:56.150
We should just go live on a
boat in some guy's backyard.

14:56.185 --> 14:58.419
So, you gonna do
that wrestling stuff?

14:58.454 --> 15:00.354
Nah, I'm gonna
stick with these.

15:00.389 --> 15:03.157
I would crime
for more of these.

15:04.694 --> 15:06.794
Okay, now if you're gonna defeat
your sister in the ring,

15:06.829 --> 15:08.662
you got to get to the root
of your fears.

15:08.698 --> 15:10.531
We got to go back
to your childhood,

15:10.566 --> 15:12.299
so I'm gonna
hypnotize you.

15:12.335 --> 15:14.535
Okay, go back.

15:14.570 --> 15:16.904
Now, we need to go
back in time.

15:19.742 --> 15:21.709
My jeans are husky.

15:21.744 --> 15:23.844
Okay, further. Further.

15:23.880 --> 15:25.479
Little further.

15:25.514 --> 15:28.048
Now, open your eyes
and tell me what you see.

15:28.084 --> 15:31.585
I see the six
stations of the Lord's order,

15:31.621 --> 15:33.888
and they will all burn!

15:33.923 --> 15:35.322
Okay, too far!
Too far! Too far!

15:35.358 --> 15:36.624
Come back. Come back.

15:36.659 --> 15:37.958
Come back.

15:37.994 --> 15:39.927
Hey,
can I make my husky jeans

15:39.962 --> 15:41.695
into cutoffs
for swimming?

15:41.731 --> 15:43.097
Ah, forget it. You're ready.

15:43.132 --> 15:45.132
Yeah, Peter.
I think you're gonna win!

15:45.167 --> 15:47.568
All right! Hey, thanks for
all your help, you guys.

15:47.603 --> 15:49.003
You know, there's
only two things

15:49.038 --> 15:50.537
I've wanted to do
my whole life:

15:50.573 --> 15:53.874
put my sister in her place
and go to Chico's Monkey Farm.

15:53.910 --> 15:54.875
♪ ♪

15:54.911 --> 15:57.244
♪ Chico's Monkey Farm ♪

15:57.280 --> 15:59.246
♪ Come and have
a howling good time ♪

15:59.282 --> 16:01.248
