<i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh, aah-aah-aah! ♪</i>

16:31.948 --> 16:35.249
<i> Chico's Monkey Farm!
Now open pending how it goes.</i>

16:47.563 --> 16:50.331
And we've got quite a match
tonight between Heavy Flo

16:50.366 --> 16:51.999
and another woman
whose name I've forgotten

16:52.034 --> 16:53.634
but I'm sure is a gross pun.

16:53.669 --> 16:55.069
Right you are, Bill.

16:55.104 --> 16:57.972
Tonight, she's up against
Her Vajesty's Secret Cervix.

16:58.007 --> 17:00.240
Interesting fact:
these two gals have

17:00.276 --> 17:02.743
over eight meters of
ass crack between them.

17:02.778 --> 17:04.478
One! Two! Three!

17:05.581 --> 17:06.981
It's over!

17:07.016 --> 17:12.553
And once again, a Heavy Flo has
ruined another lady's evening!

17:14.090 --> 17:16.323
You ain't no champ!

17:16.359 --> 17:18.525
Not till you go through me!

17:18.561 --> 17:19.860
Who the hell are you?!

17:19.895 --> 17:23.364
I'm Maxi Paddy, which is
short for Maxine Patricia.

17:23.399 --> 17:25.766
I was named after my father,
Maxwell Patrick.

17:25.801 --> 17:27.034
But that's enough about me.

17:27.069 --> 17:28.836
I'm here to kick your ass!

17:28.871 --> 17:30.070
Get out of here!

17:30.106 --> 17:32.573
I'm not fighting some fat loser
from the crowd.

17:32.608 --> 17:35.576
Huh. It looks like
this Heavy Flo is pee,

17:35.611 --> 17:37.611
because you're yellow!

17:37.646 --> 17:38.879
Oh!

17:38.914 --> 17:40.180
Well, that didn't
quite track,

17:40.216 --> 17:42.149
but the crowd
seems to be on board.

17:42.184 --> 17:43.184
It sure does!

17:43.219 --> 17:45.519
Looks like Heavy Flo
has a challenger!

17:45.554 --> 17:47.788
All right, get up here,
but make it quick.

17:47.823 --> 17:50.391
<i>I got a Lampoon
reunion to get to.</i>

17:50.426 --> 17:52.159
Heavy Flo, always
finding a way

17:52.194 --> 17:54.461
to drop her Harvard degree
into conversation.

17:54.497 --> 17:56.330
Yes, very
off-putting, Bill.

17:56.365 --> 17:59.233
Those of us who went to Harvard
really don't appreciate it.

18:05.374 --> 18:06.874
Ow! Damn it, Karen!

18:06.909 --> 18:07.975
Karen?

18:08.010 --> 18:09.243
Peter, is that you?

18:09.278 --> 18:10.511
What are you doing here?

18:10.546 --> 18:13.180
Something I should have done
a long time ago.

18:13.215 --> 18:16.050
I'm tired of you bullying me!
You're going down!

18:16.085 --> 18:17.217
Butt-scratcher?!

18:17.253 --> 18:18.519
Butt-scratcher!

18:18.554 --> 18:20.421
♪ ♪

18:45.514 --> 18:48.482
D-D-D-Don't, K-K-Karen!

18:48.517 --> 18:51.251
Toxic Shock! Toxic Shock!

18:53.322 --> 18:55.589
Oh, my God,
she's taking it too far!

18:55.624 --> 18:57.891
Heavy Flo is gonna break
this girl's arms!

18:57.927 --> 18:58.992
Woman's arms.

18:59.028 --> 19:00.294
Come on, Bill.

19:00.329 --> 19:02.329
N-N-No!

19:02.364 --> 19:04.431
Tell... Stewie...

19:04.467 --> 19:06.733
he's in charge of the show now.

19:09.271 --> 19:12.506
Say hello to Teen LaQueefa!

19:13.542 --> 19:16.510
One! Two! Three!

19:17.813 --> 19:19.012
I don't believe it!

19:19.048 --> 19:22.349
Heavy Flo is down, and
we have a new champion!

19:22.384 --> 19:24.485
I tell you, this is
one for the books,

19:24.520 --> 19:26.620
if anyone kept track
of this nonsense!

19:26.655 --> 19:29.022
Wow, you really
saved me!

19:29.058 --> 19:30.190
Thanks, stranger.

19:30.226 --> 19:31.859
Dad, it's me.

19:31.894 --> 19:34.394
Meg?

19:34.430 --> 19:36.296
It was you who saved me?

19:36.332 --> 19:37.764
That's right, Dad.

19:37.800 --> 19:40.400
Wow, even after all the
crummy stuff I've done to you?

19:40.436 --> 19:42.536
But why?
Because you're my dad.

19:42.571 --> 19:44.938
And I couldn't stand by
and watch you get hurt.

19:44.974 --> 19:46.507
Wow. Thanks, Meg.

19:46.542 --> 19:48.509
You know, that's something
even my own mom and dad

19:48.544 --> 19:49.776
never did for me.

19:49.812 --> 19:52.012
They just stood by and
let Karen pick on me.

19:52.047 --> 19:54.548
Well, you deserve better.
We all do.

19:54.583 --> 19:56.817
You know, Meg, I'm really sorry

19:56.852 --> 19:59.052
I treated you so badly
over the years.

19:59.088 --> 20:01.989
I guess I was taking out
all the pain I felt on you.

20:02.024 --> 20:05.425
I understand.
Better than anybody.

20:05.461 --> 20:07.427
But I still love you, Dad.

20:07.463 --> 20:09.429
I love you, too, Meg.

20:13.669 --> 20:17.538
Did somebody order
a hot-ass bitch and this lady?

20:17.573 --> 20:19.006
Oh, you're alive.

20:19.041 --> 20:21.175
Sorry, I was told
I was in charge now.

20:21.210 --> 20:22.976
Well, if you die,
this is kind of

20:23.012 --> 20:25.579
the creative direction
I'm leaning toward.

20:29.485 --> 20:31.118
Well, I'm proud of you, Dad.

20:31.153 --> 20:32.920
You finally stood up
for yourself.

20:32.955 --> 20:35.022
So, Peter,
have you talked to Karen?

20:35.057 --> 20:38.058
I called, like, four times, but
she's not out of the coma yet.

20:38.093 --> 20:39.593
Apparently, they usually
use fake chairs,

20:39.628 --> 20:41.028
but Meg used a real one.

20:41.063 --> 20:42.529
Do they think
she's gonna survive?

20:42.565 --> 20:44.131
It could go either way.

20:44.166 --> 20:48.945
Hello? No, I think I'm a
different blood type.

20:49.045 --> 20:51.276
No, I don't
want to check.

20:51.376 --> 20:53.409
Doctor says there's
nothing they can do.

20:53.444 --> 20:56.445
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru